{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BodyOrderCumulant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BodyOrderCumulant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_fourBody","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_fourBody","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BodyOrderCumulant.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Non-vacuity / extraction.** A genuine 4-body binding `c·C(A,4)` has connected\n4-body cumulant exactly `c`. So `fourthDiff` is a real cumulant extractor (not\nidentically zero), and the missing ⁴He `b₄` demands an irreducibly 4-body object —\nno 1- or 2-body form (the two orthogonality lemmas above) can supply it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_pairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_pairwise","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BodyOrderCumulant.lean#L42-L47","doc":"**Orthogonality (2-body).** A 2-body-ADDITIVE binding proportional to the pair\ncount (here `b·A(A−1) = 2·C(A,2)·b`, integer form to avoid division) has connected\n4-body cumulant `0`. This is `B_sym`'s bond-additive structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff_linear","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BodyOrderCumulant.lean#L37-L40","doc":"**Orthogonality (1-body).** A 1-body-LINEAR binding `B_vol(A) = a·A` has\nconnected 4-body cumulant `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fourthDiff","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BodyOrderCumulant.lean#L32-L35","doc":"The connected 4-body cumulant of a binding sequence `B : ℕ → R`, as the 4th\nforward finite difference at 0 (Newton binomial transform, 0/1-body dropped):\n`b₄ = B(4) − 4·B(3) + 6·B(2) − 4·B(1) + B(0)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}